# Portfolio 5: Distributed and Cloud Database Exercise

## Case Study
EliZeta Group is a simulated e-commerce organisation operating six retail stores in Spain. This activity continues the same case study used throughout the database portfolio.

## Objective
The objective is to examine how a cloud-hosted database can support a multi-store organisation and evaluate important distributed database concepts.

## Cloud Platform
Supabase was used to host the PostgreSQL database. The database contains the stores, products, customers, orders and order items developed in the earlier portfolio activities.

## Areas Covered
- Cloud database hosting and access.
- Multi-store data management.
- Database replication and its purpose.
- Data sharding and possible distribution strategies.
- Availability and consistency considerations.
- Benefits and limitations of cloud database services.

## Evidence and Implementation
This portfolio will include SQL-based evidence of multi-store data retrieval, cloud platform evidence and a discussion of distributed database architecture.

## Important Scope Note
The existing Supabase PostgreSQL project demonstrates cloud-hosted database usage. Replication and sharding are evaluated as architectural concepts; they are not claimed as manually configured features unless supported by implementation evidence.

## Technology
- Supabase
- PostgreSQL
- SQL

